{
  "title": "Pixelfed \u2014 social (6,976\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Pixelfed\nDomain: social | Scale: large | Stars: 6,976\nProblem: Pixelfed provides a decentralized, federated photo-sharing platform that allows users to share photos without algorithmic manipulation or centralized control. It connects with the broader fediverse via ActivityPub, enabling cross-platform social interactions.\nTarget users: Casual photographers, Creative photographers, Privacy-conscious social media users, Fediverse / decentralized web enthusiasts, Self-hosters and instance administrators\nCore features: Photo and media sharing with albums/galleries; ActivityPub federation with fediverse platforms; User profiles, following, and social feed; Real-time notifications and messaging via WebSockets; Content moderation and admin controls; Blurhash-based sensitive content previews; HLS/P2P video media support; Localization and multi-language support via Crowdin\nIntegrations: ActivityPub (fediverse federation), Pusher / Laravel Echo (WebSockets), hCaptcha, DigitalOcean Spaces (CDN/storage), Fastly CDN, PeerTube P2P media loader, YunoHost, Crowdin (localization), Patreon, NLnet Foundation\nTech stack: Vue 2, Bootstrap-Vue, Vuex, Vue Router + PHP / Laravel + MySQL/PostgreSQL (Laravel Eloquent ORM implied) + Docker, Laravel Mix, DigitalOcean Spaces, Fastly CDN\nKey libraries: laravel-echo, pusher-js, hls.js, @peertube/p2p-media-loader-core, blurhash, chart.js, plyr, bootstrap, axios, vue-masonry-css, @hcaptcha/vue-hcaptcha\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- ActivityPub federation is a first-class concern, enabling interoperability with the broader fediverse ecosystem rather than building a walled garden.\n- The project uses a classic Laravel monolith with a Vue 2 SPA frontend compiled via Laravel Mix, keeping backend and frontend tightly coupled within a single deployable unit.\n- Real-time features (notifications, live feeds) are handled through Laravel Echo and Pusher, decoupling WebSocket infrastructure from the core application.\n- Blurhash and P2P media loading (HLS/PeerTube) are integrated to optimize media delivery UX and reduce server bandwidth costs at scale.",
